keetna's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Talkeetna has set <strong class=\"sig\">9 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 92 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">149 record highs</strong>, far more than the 92 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (71). Talkeetna's all-time high is 96\u00b0F, on June 17, 2013.","t_chg":"Talkeetna's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 98 complete years: Talkeetna's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.67\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.51 to +0.83), about +6.9\u00b0F since 1921. Talkeetna's average high shows no clear change: +0.10\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.05 to +0.25) that includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 9 of 12 months. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Talkeetna's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.35 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 26.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 1929 (45.21 in); the driest, 1969 (15.50 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 1 daily record high, 1 daily record low"}}